    fix: don't block main loop for WiFi reconnect on Core2

    The background maintain_connection() path (added in 3.4.2) could block
    loop() for ~3.3-3.8s per retry on Core2, since connect_wifi()'s
    wait_for_connection() verify-loop stacked on top of Core2's extra
    esp_wifi_stop()/start() delays. That starved M5.update(), making menu
    touch buttons appear unresponsive whenever a reconnect was attempted
    and failed (e.g. device ID configured but WiFi credentials wrong).

    connect_wifi() now takes a wait_for_result flag; the automatic
    background path fires the attempt without waiting, while user-initiated
    connects from the WiFi settings screen keep the bounded wait.

    Bump to 3.4.3.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 60a286a6d2e9

